// Title: Osacompile Execution By Potentially Suspicious Applet/Osascript
// Sigma ID: a753a6af-3126-426d-8bd0-26ebbcb92254
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Sohan G (D4rkCiph3r), Red Canary (Idea)
// Date: 2023-04-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.002
// Description: Detects potential suspicious applet or osascript executing "osacompile".
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/mac-application-bundles/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_suspicious_applet_behaviour.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/applet" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/osascript") and ProcessCommandLine contains "osacompile"
